login present at any point in the post-restart check.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2916984835eb4fd6\",\"cmd-167d55266700480a\",\"cmd-0a7123508ae8410c\",\"cmd-cc934ba69dd743a1\",\"cmd-1d2f6595514c4db7\",\"cmd-7f60a36e1ee641fe\",\"global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity\",\"global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.92,\"summary\":\"Reviewing the chronological command trace, all state-changing actions map to a clear purpose: package install, user creation, linger enablement, image pull, and Quadlet unit creation/start are all necessary prerequisites or the final solution itself; the reboot was the required verification step for the boot/no-session requirement. Two commands failed (cmd-dba215417461488c: an attempt to use podman generate systemd after stopping/removing the ad hoc test container, and cmd-7d30f298ce744a1f: an attempt to systemctl --user enable --now a Quadlet-generated transient unit) but neither left residue - the generate/mv sequence failed cleanly with no file written, and the enable attempt failed with no state change, immediately corrected by a plain start in cmd-ec66366f815f4e5b. The one manual podman run test container (cmd-016da942b6c047a2) was deliberately stopped and removed before the Quadlet unit took over, so it left no lingering duplicate service. The after_executor lifecycle snapshot shows no failed systemd units and no unexpected listening sockets beyond the intended 8080 (plus normal DHCP/DNS churn from the reboot), and package health is unaffected.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-dba215417461488c\",\"cmd-7d30f298ce744a1f\",\"cmd-016da942b6c047a2\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All three material outcomes of the task - an unprivileged rootless-podman container, serving on port 8080, that starts at boot with appsvc having no active login session - are directly and coherently demonstrated, including a full pre-restart baseline / disruption / boot-identity change / post-restart recovery cycle that satisfies the stricter evidentiary bar for boot/availability-related claims. Two transient command failures during setup were harmless and were promptly corrected without leaving residue, and lifecycle snapshots show no unwanted mutations, failed services, or package damage.\",\"limitations\":[\"Only a single reboot cycle was captured; repeatability of boot-start behavior across multiple reboots is not directly evidenced.\",\"The provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol and the task's own boot-start requirement overlap in this task, so the same reboot evidence serves both purposes; no separate restart evidence gap exists here.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run a containerized web app as the unprivileged appsvc account via rootless podman","status":"satisfied","summary":"appsvc created as a normal (non-root) user with subuid/subgid ranges; podman info run as appsvc confirms Rootless=true; the container is defined and managed via a Podman Quadlet unit (webapp.container) placed under appsvc's own systemd --user config, and the resulting webapp.service runs the nginx:alpine container under appsvc's user session/slice (user@1000.service, user.slice/user-1000.slice), never as root.","evidence_ids":["cmd-bb6b8054ef094495","cmd-961168936644430b","cmd-0593bf74fcfa49d1","cmd-ec66366f815f4e5b"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"App serves on port 8080","status":"satisfied","summary":"curl to node1:8080 returned HTTP 200 both immediately after the manual test run and after the Quadlet unit was started, and again after the full reboot. The after-executor listening-sockets snapshot independently confirms a listener on *:8080 owned by rootlessport (the rootless podman port-forwarder), corroborating the curl results with a state-based observation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9fb14985a8be4dd0","cmd-0a11c2bf9b